# NOTE (appended after the run, 2026-11-02T02:40:39Z): stopped at step 1b. Two findings: (1) harness bug: the reset check read the exit code of 'pft-mounts audit | tail -1' through ssh (tail's 0); (2) REAL tool bug: rollback unmounted the /tmp and /var/tmp self-binds before restoring fstab + daemon-reload, and systemd mounted its fstab-generator tmp.mount/var-tmp.mount again 1 s later (12 findings instead of 11: /tmp, /var/tmp noexec live but not persistent). Fixed in the next commit (fstab + daemon-reload first, every unmount verified); manual reset of the sentry in log 08.
